    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0398" n="378" xml:id="pg378"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 55.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 21, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 26th of November last,
                    No. 59, has been received. I have learned with much satisfaction of the friendly
                    dispositions manifested towards the United States by your diplomatic colleagues
                    at Peking. Your letter to Sir Frederick Bruce, in acknowledgment of the course
                    pursued by him in regard to the Osborne flotilla, is approved and commended; and
                    I shall request Mr. Adams to make a further expression at London of the
                    estimation in which Sir Frederick’s conduct is held by this government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD,</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
